# BuildKit reads `<dockerfile>.dockerignore` beside the Dockerfile in preference to the
# context root's `.dockerignore`. Both CI (`-f deployment/governance-studio/Dockerfile .`)
# and a managed host build this image with the REPOSITORY ROOT as the context, where the root
# `.dockerignore` (`*` plus a re-include of `symbolu/` only, written for the GKE controller
# image) excludes every path this Dockerfile COPYs. This file is that same exclusion set, in
# the one place the build actually reads it. Keep it identical to `.dockerignore` beside it.
# Keep secrets, VCS metadata, test/build cruft and node_modules out of the image.
.git
.gitignore
**/.git
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/.vite
**/coverage
**/playwright-report
**/test-results
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
**/.pytest_cache
**/.mypy_cache
**/.env
**/*.env
**/.env.*
deployment/governance-studio/tests/certs
**/artifacts/dependency-audit-report.json
*.key
*.pem
